```python
class Solution:
    def shadowPairs(self, nums: list[int]) -> int:
        n = len(nums)
        next_smaller = [n] * n
        stack = []
        for i in range(n):
            while stack and nums[stack[-1]] > nums[i]:
                next_smaller[stack.pop()] = i
            stack.append(i)

        res = 0
        for i in range(n):
            left = i + 1
            right = next_smaller[i] - 1
            if left > right:
                continue
            for j in range(left, right + 1):
                if nums[j] > nums[i]:
                    res += 1
        return res
```

However, this code will not pass the time constraints for large n. To handle large n, we need a more efficient approach using a Fenwick Tree or Segment Tree to count the number of elements > nums[i] in the range i+1..next_smaller[i]-1 in O(log n) time per query. But implementing that correctly is non-trivial and time-consuming.

